  "releaseNotes": "**DI019 provider guards**: root and scoped provider aliases guarded with `?? throw` now keep their provider classification, avoiding missed root scoped resolutions and stale false positives after reassignment. | **DI019 scope-wrapping code fix**: fixes inside `lock` bodies now emit synchronous `using` / `CreateScope()` output instead of illegal `await using` statements, while top-level `Program.cs` local declarations now use sync or async scopes to match the top-level body when the resolved service does not escape.",
